;; The lockstep (AX5-DESIGN §3, AXS56 (a)-AXS58 (a), AX5.3): the executable run natively under ptrace (ASLR off) and on
;; x86i from the native's own initial state (its stack's bytes, the vdso's auxv entry made AT_IGNORE in both).
;;
;; The sys mode compares at each system call's entry (the registers but RAX, RCX and R11; the number; RIP; the flags the last
;; instruction defined; FS's base) and exit (the result). The step mode single-steps the native process and compares after
;; every instruction: the sixteen registers, RIP, the flags the last flag-setting instruction defined (AXS72 (a): its own
;; undefined bits, not a family's; the native's undefined bits then copied into x86i so the two stay one state), FS's and
;; GS's bases, the bytes the instruction stored (read back from the native at the addresses x86i stored them), XMM and MXCSR
;; when the instruction names an XMM register, and at each system call and every 4,096 instructions the writable mappings.
;; The bisection runs the sys mode, and from the last system call both agreed on, the step mode, naming the first
;; differing instruction.
;;
;; Both modes copy the world's calls' results and buffers from the native (time, random, ids, uname, affinity); the sys
;; mode also takes the addresses mmap and brk return from it, the step mode checks x86i's own choice against them (the
;; layout). cpuid's native answer is overwritten with x86i's model's, rdtsc's taken from the native. The loader's judge
;; compares x86i's own initial stack (emu.Stack, the native's AT_RANDOM bytes given) with the native's at its exec.



(go/var ^{:doc "world are the calls whose results x86i copies from the native (AXS58 (a)): number -> the argument that is the output\nbuffer and its size (-1: the result's count of bytes; 0: no buffer).\n"} world (lit (map uint64 (array 2 int))
    ^{:line 35} [228 (lit _ 1 16)] ; clock_gettime(clk, ts)
    ^{:line 36} [96 (lit _ 0 16)] ; gettimeofday(tv, tz)
    ^{:line 37} [201 (lit _ 0 8)] ; time(t)
    ^{:line 38} [318 (lit _ 0 -1)] ; getrandom(buf, len, flags)
    ^{:line 39} [39 (lit _ -1 0)] ; getpid
    ^{:line 40} [186 (lit _ -1 0)] ; gettid
    ^{:line 41} [110 (lit _ -1 0)] ; getppid
    ^{:line 42} [63 (lit _ 0 390)] ; uname
    ^{:line 43} [204 (lit _ 2 -1)])) ; sched_getaffinity(pid, len, mask)


(go/var regNames (lit (array 16 string) "RAX" "RCX" "RDX" "RBX" "RSP" "RBP" "RSI" "RDI" "R8" "R9" "R10" "R11" "R12" "R13" "R14" "R15"))

